# Configuration and Security Rules (WatchAgent)

- Do not commit real API keys, credentials, tokens, private URLs, or personal
  secrets. This project should run with the public Open-Meteo API and local
  SQLite by default.
- New runtime settings must be read through `app/config.py`, documented in
  `.env.example`, and explained in README when they affect setup or behavior.
- Keep Docker startup clean-clone friendly: `cp .env.example .env` followed by
  `docker compose up --build` should remain sufficient.
- Keep the container non-root unless there is a documented reason to change it.
- Do not log secrets or full untrusted upstream payloads. Log city, status,
  timeout, and short diagnostic details instead.
- Network calls must keep explicit timeouts and raise typed weather-client
  errors that the poller can log without stopping other cities.
